Which pair identifies the normal curve with the largest mean and the normal curve with the largest standard deviation? The curves use the same axes.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.55cm,y=0.8cm]
\draw[->] (-8,0)--(8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[thick] plot[domain=-7.8:7.8,samples=120] (\x,{exp(-\x*\x/8)});
\draw[thick,dashed] plot[domain=-1.5:5.5,samples=90] (\x,{2*exp(-(\x-2)^2/2)});
\draw[thick,dotted] plot[domain=-3.75:-0.25,samples=90] (\x,{4*exp(-2*(\x+2)^2)});
\node at (0,1.3) {$A$};
\node at (2,2.3) {$B$};
\node at (-2,4.3) {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
